# Daily live portfolio run.
#
# 09:30 EVERY calendar day, America/New_York (TZ is set in the image, so this is ET not UTC).
# The futures book runs seven days a week (HD 2026-09-17; T-5): the Saturday run books and trades
# the Friday session, the Sunday run carries the book over the closed Saturday, and the Monday run
# books the Sunday Globex session. A Mon-Fri schedule drops a session a week and breaks the T-1
# chain (T-5 measured it: a phantom rebuild every Monday, or, under the run-gap guard, a refusal
# from the first Monday on). The engine decides per symbol whether T-1 was a session; the
# schedule does not.
#
# Output goes to /proc/1/fd/1 -- the container's stdout -- so `docker logs
# trade-ngin` shows every run and every failure. The previous version wrote to
# /var/log/cron.log inside the container, where three months of daily failures
# accumulated unseen.
30 9 * * * /app/scripts/run_live_portfolio.sh >> /proc/1/fd/1 2>&1
